## 4. Standardization and Data Type Rules

All values arrive as text. A value that cannot be converted becomes null and is then handled by C-03 (rejected with reason `unparseable_value`); it is never guessed.

### 4.1 Data Types and Formats

| Rule ID | Columns | Standard format / type | On failure |
|---|---|---|---|
| S-01 | `updated_at`, `sale_date`, `expense_date` | DATETIME `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS` | Reject (C-03) |
| S-02 | `quantity` | INTEGER | Reject (C-03) |
| S-03 | All IDs, `recorded_by`, `sales.stock_id` | INTEGER | Reject (C-03) |
| S-04 | `unit_price`, `amount` | DECIMAL(10,2) and DECIMAL(12,2) | Reject (C-03) |
| S-05 | `stocks.size` | Upper case `CHB-<number>` | Reject (`invalid_size_pattern`) |
| S-06 | `stocks.unit` | Lower case, mapped (e.g. `pcs`) | Reject (`unmapped_unit`) |
| S-07 | `customer_name`, `shop_name`, `category` | Title Case | Not applicable |
| S-08 | `sales.phone_number` | Digits only, 7 to 15 digits | Set `Unknown` (C-04) |
| S-09 | All text columns | Maximum length (Section 6) | Reject (`exceeds_length`) |
| S-10 | `sales_id`, `expenses_id` | Renamed `sale_id`, `expense_id` | V-02 fails |
| S-11 | `expenses.description` | Trimmed only, casing kept | Not applicable |

**Conversion details**

- **S-01 dates:** accepted source formats are `YYYY-MM-DD`, `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM[:SS]`, `YYYY/MM/DD`, `MM/DD/YYYY [time]`, `DD/MM/YYYY` (only if the first part is above 12), and `Mon DD, YYYY [time]`. A date without a time becomes `00:00:00`. Time zone is Asia/Manila with no conversion.
- **S-02 quantity:** remove thousands separators and the text `pcs` or `pc`. `100.0` becomes `100`; `100.5` is not whole and fails.
- **S-04 prices:** remove `₱`, `PHP`, `Php`, `P`, spaces, and comma separators, then round half up to 2 decimals. A comma followed by 1 or 2 final digits (`12,50`) is not accepted.
- **S-05 size:** `chb-4`, `CHB4`, and `CHB 4` all become `CHB-4`.
- **S-07 names:** each word after a space or hyphen is capitalized, so `juan DELA cruz` becomes `Juan Dela Cruz`.
- **S-08 phone:** stored as text so a leading `0` is kept. `0917-123-4567` becomes `09171234567`.

**Date ambiguity (S-01).** A slash date with both parts 12 or below (e.g. `03/04/2026`) is read month-first. If that reading falls outside the batch window and the day-first reading falls inside it, the day-first reading is used and the row counts under S-01. If neither reading is inside the window, the row is rejected by C-10. Two-digit years are not accepted.

**Numeric precision and rounding.** Exact decimal arithmetic (Python `Decimal`), never floating point. Rounding is half up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`) to 2 decimal places.

**Currency.** All money is Philippine peso (PHP). The currency is implicit and no currency column is stored. Units of measure are `pcs` unless the reference table lists others. Country or region codes are not used.

### 4.2 Reference Values (`config/reference_values.csv`)

| Column | Source variants | Standard value |
|---|---|---|
| `unit` | `pcs`, `pc`, `pc.`, `pcs.`, `piece`, `pieces` (any casing) | `pcs` |
| `category` | Owner-defined variants, e.g. a synonym list per category | Standard category in Title Case. A category that is not listed is **kept** in Title Case, not rejected. |

The Owner maintains the file. Any change is a change of rules version (Section 8).

