## 5. Business Transformation Rules

### 5.1 Derived Columns, Lookups, and Filters

| Rule ID | Input columns | Logic or formula | Output column | Business reason |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| B-01 | `sales.quantity`, `sales.unit_price` | `total_amount = ROUND_HALF_UP(quantity * unit_price, 2)` using exact decimals, computed after cleaning and type conversion | `sales.total_amount` DECIMAL(12,2) | Revenue per sale line. The source `total_amount` is never accepted; this is the only place it is created. |
| B-02 | `sales.stock_id` | Lookup (existence check) against `stocks.stock_id` of this batch plus existing `blockflow.db` stock IDs; unmatched rows are rejected by C-08 | none (validation only) | A sale must refer to a real stock item |
| B-03 | `recorded_by` (all tables) | Lookup against `users.user_id` (read-only); unmatched rows are rejected by C-08 | none (validation only) | Every record must be traceable to a real user |

```text
total_amount = quantity x unit_price      (rounded half up to 2 decimals)
```

If a source file still contains a `total_amount` column, it is dropped at extraction, and it is never compared or reused here.

### 5.2 Rules That Do Not Apply (stated explicitly)

| Topic | Decision | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| Joins | None. B-02 and B-03 are existence lookups on a unique key list and never add rows or columns. | No table needs to be combined in this stage |
| Aggregations | None | Output is at record level; daily totals or profit would be added as new B-rules before they are built |
| Business exclusions (e.g. cancelled records) | None. The source has no status column. Every valid record is kept. | The only exclusions are data-quality rejects (Section 3), each counted and logged |
| Dimensional modeling, surrogate keys, SCD | Not used. `blockflow.db` is an operational database, so source IDs remain the primary keys and no `dim_`/`fact_` tables are built. | Avoids changing the Stage 1 model; no history tracking is required |